    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="reference-handler-shape" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/">IJobHandler exemplar.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor level (FULL) and load knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Author H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs — inject IKeyVaultCertClient, IGraphAppOnlyClient, IPowerShellRunner, IDataverseWebApiClient, ICosmosRunStore, IIdempotencyService.</step>
    <step order="2">Load confidential-client cert from customer KV (path: customer-{customerId}-spe-bootstrap-cert or platform equivalent).</step>
    <step order="3">Acquire app-only Graph token with cert; assert public-client token flow is NOT used (§4B T6 verification).</step>
    <step order="4">Invoke hardened Create-NewContainerType.ps1 + Register-*.ps1 + New-BusinessUnitContainer.ps1 with the app-only token.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify container GET via app-only token returns 200.</step>
    <step order="6">Persist containerId to sprk_SharePointEmbeddedContainerId (Dataverse env-var) AND KV secret customer-{customerId}-spe-container-id.</step>
    <step order="7">Write containerTypeId to Cosmos interStepState.</step>
    <step order="8">Author unit tests: (a) happy path — T6 verified (confidential-client used), (b) delegated-token accidental use = fail with trap-T6 code, (c) container GET fails post-create = deploy fail, (d) idempotency.</step>
    <step order="9">Register in L2 Program.cs DI.</step>
    <step order="10">Run dotnet build + dotnet test; verify green + zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change task 051 status from 🔲 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviations in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If SPE container-type replication does NOT complete within the customer-declared 24h lead-time window (H0 preflight said cert-bootstrap done, but replication is still pending), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT retry-loop; this indicates a Microsoft-side incident or a customer-prereq gap.</trigger>
    <trigger>If confidential-client cert is missing from KV at H8 start (indicates Phase B cert-bootstrap script missed or H4 didn't populate the cert), STOP and escalate — do NOT invent a fallback token acquisition path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: scripts/Create-NewContainerType.ps1 + related scripts (Phase B hardened to confidential-client). No existing L2 handler.</existing>
    <extension>No — the PS scripts must be invocable with app-only token loaded from KV cert, resumable, and gate-verified per T6 post-condition. Ad-hoc invocation of the scripts breaks T6 trap owner semantics.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without H8 owning T6 verification, a delegated-token slip would silently 403 with "public client not allowed" mid-run, leaving the customer environment without a container. H8 without T6 owner = the exact silent-fail that T6 catalogs.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run az CLI for KV cert operations</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H8SpeContainerTypeHandler.Tests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given cert present in KV and SPE replication complete (verified in H0 preflight), when HandleAsync runs, then container-type + root container are created and container GET via app-only token returns 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T6 (spec.md FR-33): confidential-client (app-only) token acquisition is used; if any code path attempts delegated-token flow, deploy fails with trap-T6 code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-condition: containerId persisted to Dataverse env-var sprk_SharePointEmbeddedContainerId AND KV secret customer-{customerId}-spe-container-id (both writes verified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency: two invocations for the same customerId — second call is a no-op (spe-{customerId} match); scripts skip existing container-type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: H8 invoked without tenantId parameter returns failure (§4D I5); Graph token acquisition uses target tenant tid explicitly, never MI default tenant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: container ID is stored ONLY at the tenant-scoped storage locations (Dataverse env-var + KV secret with customer-scoped name); no fallback default location.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Graph SDK calls catch ODataError (NFR-09 net10 Kiota 2.0).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Handler registers in L2 DI; dotnet build + dotnet test exit 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-11 + FR-33 (T6) + MUST rules + NFR-09 + §4D I4/I5; design.md §4.1 H8 (v3.3 SPE privilege footnote) + §4B T6. Phase B cert-bootstrap script hardening is a prerequisite.

